(a) SMPL-X left elbow local axes (rest T-pose, palms down; body forward = +z, up = +y)
  rotvec x +90: wrist moves   33.0 mm, direction [ 0.   -0.63  0.78]
  rotvec y -90: wrist moves  356.4 mm, direction [-0.7   0.    0.71]
  rotvec z +90: wrist moves  357.9 mm, direction [-0.77  0.64  0.  ]
  -> local x ~ forearm axis (twist), local -y swings forearm forward (+z) = flexion, local z swings it up/down = varus/valgus. SMPLify's angle prior uses the same convention (penalises +y on left elbow).
